  "issue_number": 123,
  "issue_title": "feat(data): add contributor reconciliation reports",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n- add private contributor reconciliation reports\n- compare official contributor totals with cached GitHub context\n- separate maintainer-lane history from normal contributor evidence\n\n## What changed\n- builds per-repo official, cached, and effective totals\n- explains mismatch reasons such as lookback, stale/closed context, unavailable official data, and maintainer-owned history\n- threads reconciliation into contributor outcome history with deterministic ordering\n- keeps readiness integration fixtures current so freshness SLO assertions remain deterministic in CI\n\n## Why\n- private decision data should explain why official and cached GitHub histories differ without inflating contributor evidence.\n\n## Validation\n- git diff --check\n- npx tsc --noEmit\n- npx vitest run test/unit/signals-v2.test.ts\n- npm run test:coverage\n- GitHub validate, Contributor trust, and Superagent Security Scan pass on the latest head\n\nCloses #108",
